MULTICLOUD DEVSECOPS PLATFORM

Complete End-to-End Project Documentation

AWS + Google Cloud | Terraform | Jenkins | Docker | Kubernetes | Helm | SonarQube | OWASP Dependency-Check | Trivy | Prometheus | Grafana

Project: multicloud-devsecops-platform

CI/CD Design: One parameterized Jenkins pipeline

Pipeline Parameter: CLOUD_PROVIDER = AWS or GCP

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Project Overview
The Multicloud DevSecOps Platform is an end-to-end cloud-native CI/CD project that builds, tests, scans, containerizes and deploys a Spring Boot application to either Amazon EKS or Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE) using a single parameterized Jenkins pipeline. 

Terraform provisions the cloud infrastructure, Jenkins manages the CI/CD workflow, Docker provides containerization, Helm manages Kubernetes deployments, SonarQube performs source-code quality analysis, OWASP Dependency-Check analyzes third-party dependencies, Trivy scans container images, and Prometheus/Grafana provide Kubernetes and application workload monitoring.

The same Jenkins pipeline supports both cloud providers through the CLOUD_PROVIDER parameter.

Core Components
•	Infrastructure as Code: Terraform
•	CI/CD: Jenkins Declarative Pipeline
•	Application: Spring Boot application
•	Build: Maven
•	Containerization: Docker
•	AWS Registry: Amazon ECR
•	AWS Kubernetes: Amazon EKS
•	GCP Registry 
•	GCP Kubernetes: Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE)
•	Kubernetes packaging: Helm
•	Code quality/Static Analysis: SonarQube
•	Dependency Vulnerability Scanning: OWASP Dependency-Check + NVD API
•	Container Image Scanning/File System Scanning: Trivy
•	Monitoring: Prometheus and Grafana through kube-prometheus-stack 

The application source code and application/pom.xml are not modified as part of the deployment design.

