14. Security Controls

The project implements multiple security controls throughout the CI/CD workflow.

SonarQube
Used for:
•	Source-code analysis.
•	Code-quality analysis.
•	Static analysis.

OWASP Dependency-Check
Used for:
•	Third-party dependency vulnerability analysis.
•	Identification of known vulnerable dependencies.

NVD API
provides vulnerability database information used by  Dependency-Check.

Trivy
Used for: 
•	 File System scanning/container image vulnerability scanning.
Trivy scans the Docker image before the image is pushed to the selected cloud registry.

Jenkins Credentials
Used for centralized management of:
•	SonarQube token
•	NVD API Key
•	Other required credentials

Secrets are not stored in source code.

IAM and Kubernetes RBAC
Authorization is controlled through:
•	AWS IAM
•	GCP IAM
•	Kubernetes RBAC

Least-privilege permissions are recommended for production environments.

Broad permissions used during sandbox implementation should not automatically be considered a production security model.

