15. Troubleshooting

15.1 Jenkins cannot access Docker

Check Jenkins group membership
groups jenkins

Test Docker as the Jenkins user:
sudo -u jenkins docker ps

Check Docker:
sudo systemctl status docker --no-pager

If necessary:
sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins

Restart Jenkins so the Jenkins process receives the updated group membership.

-------------------------------------------------------------

15.2 Wrong Kubernetes context

Check the current context:
kubectl config current-context

Inspect the current context:
kubectl config view --minify

Verify cluster access:
kubectl get nodes

-------------------------------------------------------------

15.3 GKE container.nodes.list Forbidden

If GKE reports a missing permission such as:
container.nodes.list

Verify:
1. Which identity Jenkins is using.
2. Which Google Cloud IAM roles that identity has.
3. Whether the required IAM role contains the missing permission.
4. Whether Kubernetes RBAC is also correctly configured.

A Kubernetes ClusterRoleBinding alone may not resolve a Google Cloud IAM authorization error.

-------------------------------------------------------------

15.4 Artifact Registry Upload Denied

If the Jenkins service account cannot push an image:
1. Verify the active project.
2. Verify the Artifact Registry repository.
3. Verify the Jenkins service account.
4. Verify repository-level Artifact Registry Writer permission.

Example:
gcloud artifacts repostitories add-iam-policy-binding \
  multicloud-devsecops \
  --location=us-east-1 \
  --project-"$PROJECT_ID" \
  --member="serviceAccount:multicloud-devsecops-jenkins@$PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/artifactregistry.writer"

-------------------------------------------------------------

15.5 AWS EKS AccessDenied

If Jenkins receives an AWS access-denied error for operations such as:
eks:DescribeCluster 
eks:ListClusters 

Verify the IAM role attached to the Jenkins EC2 instance.

The required permissions should be granted through an authorized AWS administrator.

Avoid granting broad permissions when narrower permissions are sufficient.

