19. Production Recommendations
•	Use least-privilege IAM.
•	Use least-privilege Kubernetes RBAC.
•	Use separate service identitied for environments.
•	Rotate credentials and tokens.
•	Store secrets in managed secret-management systems.
• Prefer repository-level Artifact Registry permissions.
• Avoid cluster-admin access for Jenkins.
• Keep cloud project IDs and environment-specific values out of reusable documentation.
• Pin or approve Terraform provider versions.
• Pin or approve Helm chart versions.
• Pin important CI/CD tool versions.
• Define resource requests and limits.
• Configure monitoring retention according to requirements.
• Define backup and recovery policies.
• Use separate development, staging, and production environments.
• Protect production deployment branches and credentials.
• Add stronger deployment approval controls for production.
• Keep security scans and their thresholds explicitly defined in the CI/CD policy.

