20. Conclusion

The Multicloud DevSecOps Platform demonstrates a reusable cloud-native DevSecOps architecture in which a single parameterized Jenkins pipeline can deploy a Spring Boot applciation to either AWS or Google Cloud.

The implementation combines:

• Terraform Infrastructure as Code.
• Jenkins CI/CD
• Maven
• Docker
• SonarQube
• OWASP Dependency-Check
• Trivy
• Amazon ECR
• Artifact Registry
• Amazon EKS
• GKE
• Kubernetes
• Helm
• Prometheus
• Grafana

The common CI/CD stages remain shared between cloud providers, while registry authentication, Kubernetes cluster access, and cloud-specific deployment configuration are selected according to:

CLOUD_PROVIDER = AWS

or

CLOUD_PROVIDER = GCP

The monitoring implementation intentionally reports Kubernetes and application workload resource metrics. Because the current application does not expose the required HTTP server request metric, the project does not claim HTTP request-rate or response-time monitoring.

This provides an accurate representation of the implemented platform without overstating its current capabilities.